  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ISF, Acc&#xe8;s aux services d&apos;accompagnement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to provide an experience of home-based support services in order to eliminate the stigmatization of young people with multiple disabilities.
 It is about training 20 young people and their parents on the CRPD, home support techniques, communication and advocacy, so that they can themselves carry out advocacy and awareness actions towards authorities, teachers and other youngpeople.
Also, this project aims to promote home-based work for young people with multiple disabilities in orderfor them to become autonomous in certain tasks of daily life.
Finally, they will be equipped with technical or special aids and digital tablets made available to the animators that will allow them to exchange with the world.
Through this project, EWB and the rights holders intend to further address the problems of access to education and training that seriously reduce the chances of young people with two or more disabilities (blind-deaf, blind-locomotive, deaf-locomotive etc.).
Indeed, disabled children can receive support for social and educational integration in the center where they are registered. In addition, when they are unable to study in a regular school environment, they can benefit from special education services at home, which provide academic support and assistance in acquiring independence.
These young people, because of the complexity of their care, have never received special attention and remain on the margins of the national education system.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="11">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusion Sans Fronti&#xe8;re-Multi Handicap (ISF) is the result of a group of good wills, the majority of which are disabled people. Itis therefore full of experiences of living with a handicap and the fact that out of 34975 handicapped children who are of school age only 301 go to school (source SNES). Noting that the majority of disabled students end up dropping out to return to begging, giventheir precarious living conditions. Also noting that the inclusive community-based development which is nothing but a multi-sectoral approach that relies on the participation and contribution of all community actors Convinced that any remediation must take root from early age or at the grassroots, these precursors of the ISF were determined and created the Association which was authorized to carry out its activities by the decree No. 0699/MI/D/DGAPJ/DLP of 24July 2019. Inclusion Sans Fronti&#xe8;re Multi Handicap intervenes inNiger in the field of promotion and protection of disabled people who are underserved or discriminated against, namely: children with disabilities aged 0 to 5, - children with two or more disabilities, - displaced persons with disabilities and their families, - girls/women living in rural and desert areas. It also intervenes in the field of health,inclusive education, home-based work. During its last General Assembly, it oriented its intervention actions in the field of emergency situations (disaster, conflict) in connection with environmental protection and climate change. ISF is a member of the Niger Federation of Disabled Persons (FNPH) and collaborates with Ministry of National Education, Ministry of Public Health, Population and Social Reform, Ministry of Women&apos;s Promotion and Child Protection; Ministry of Environment and Desertification Control; ASBL Belgium, Info Braille, Lumi&#xe8;re des Personnes Handicap&#xe9;es,</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusion Sans Frontriere multi-han</narrative>
  </participating-org>
